      "reasons": [
        "The packet states that self-discrepancy occurs when a person’s “actual self” is distanced from their “ideal self” and “ought self,” and that behavior is motivated to reduce the gap between what the person “actually present[s]” and the ought/wish/ideal self. However, it does not explicitly define the “actual self” as how a person sees who they are at present, nor does it directly contrast “present” self-perception with “ideally want to be/feel they should be” in the way the definition claims.",
        "Because the definition’s first sentence contains an explicit meaning (“sees who they are at present”) that is not clearly supported by the provided packet text, the definition is not fully defensible from the source."
